Wind Chime Park is going to hold a "Ten Picture Badge Trial". Please design 4 badge projects first. Each project must have a name, eligibility, completion conditions, usable images, and images that should not be mixed in. Events cannot be divided simply by "whether there are people or not" or "whether it is outdoors", but must be able to distinguish different physical rules: hanging and swinging, climbing and climbing obstacles, children's free activities, formal swings or hitting balls, and logistics or spectator areas.

Then please write the 10 pictures into the trial register one by one:
- Which badge it can strive for;
- Is it a formal action, preparatory action, spectator/logistics, or violation substitution in this badge;
- If you want to connect it to the previous picture, what characters, equipment or site conditions need to be met;
- What is the maximum number of next items it can receive after that.

Finally, please provide a "Children's Main Route" and an "Adult/Formal Sports Branch". The main route for children's play must involve at least two types of swinging, climbing or free activities; the formal sports branch must explain why baseball and golf cannot be considered the same event just because they are both swings. Choose another picture that is most likely to be misjudged as a member of the main route, and explain whether the misjudgement will first destroy the age, equipment, field boundaries, or referee rules.

Add "mutually exclusive tags" in this round: write at least one condition for each major group that cannot be shared, such as different people, different sites, different tools, different process stages, different applicable objects or different risk levels. If two groups can be displayed side by side, a footnote must also be written to indicate whether they share only appearance, background, words, or a stronger task relationship. Finally, one conclusion was selected and downgraded to "can only be retained for now" to explain what kind of visual evidence is missing before it can be upgraded.

